---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const workflows = [
 {id:'prepare',number:'01',title:'Sketch a molecular structure',tools:'vibe-sketch → input files',detail:'Draw or import a structure, clean up its layout and generate a 3D geometry. Choose supported job settings and export a vibe-qc or ORCA input. Check charge, multiplicity, method and basis before running it.',output:'A structure, a publication figure or a calculation input. An input file is not a calculated result.',href:'/vibe-sketch/docs/inputs.html',label:'Read the sketcher input guide',note:'Testing version. Names and QVF saving require optional integrations; .vsk saving remains available without qvf-writer.'},
 {id:'schedule',number:'02',title:'Submit the calculation',tools:'vibe-queue · vq',detail:'Configure a local or remote host, submit the command with its input workspace, and follow the job through completion. The queue can run other command-line software as well as vibe-qc.',output:'A tracked job with its submitted inputs, requested resources and execution status.',href:'/vibe-queue/docs/user/index.html',label:'Follow the job guide',note:'Host setup and scheduler configuration belong to the queue installation. A core source build does not configure a queue.'},
 {id:'calculate',number:'03',title:'Run your first calculation',tools:'vibe-qc · Python',detail:'The engine executes the prepared input on the selected host. For a first local example, begin with a small Hartree–Fock calculation on water. Read the SCF energy and orbital energies, then use the tutorial paths to add DFT, correlation, properties or periodic boundary conditions.',output:'Energies and properties for a specified geometry and method, with convergence and calculation settings.',href:`${base}get-started#first-calculation`,label:'Run the water example',note:'Coordinates in the website example are in bohr. Always retain units, basis, charge, spin and convergence settings.'},
 {id:'explore',number:'04',title:'Analyze and share the result',tools:'vibe-view · QVF',detail:'Open a QVF archive or a supported structure and volume file. Inspect available structures, orbitals, densities and spectra; use the headless interface when you need repeatable figures.',output:'An inspected result and exported views, with the underlying archive retained.',href:'/vibe-view/docs/workflows.html',label:'Follow the viewer workflows',note:'What can be shown depends on the data in the file and the viewing interface. The viewer does not create missing calculation evidence.'},
];
---
<Base title="Scientific workflows — vibe-qc" description="Sketch a structure, submit the job, calculate its properties, then analyze the result.">
<Nav /><main id="main-content" class="wrap">
<header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Workflows</span><h1>Start with the work<br />you need to do.</h1><p>The queued workflow is sketch → submit → calculate → analyze. For a direct local run, skip submission. Each tool also works independently.</p></header>
<nav class="workflow-index" aria-label="Workflow sections">{workflows.map(w=><a href={`#${w.id}`}><span>{w.number}</span>{w.title} ↓</a>)}</nav>
{workflows.map(w=><section class="workflow-row" id={w.id}><div class="workflow-number">{w.number}</div><div><span class="eyebrow">{w.tools}</span><h2>{w.title}</h2><p>{w.detail}</p><a class="text-link" href={w.href}>{w.label} ↗</a></div><aside><h3>What you keep</h3><p>{w.output}</p><h3>Before you continue</h3><p>{w.note}</p></aside></section>)}
<section class="document-section"><div class="card"><h2>Reproducibility travels with the files.</h2><p>Keep the exact software version, geometry or cell, units, method, basis, approximations and convergence settings with your result. For a method comparison, use the same specification and the tolerances documented in the reference.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/validation.html">Read the validation evidence ↗</a></div></section>
</main><Footer /></Base>
<style>
.workflow-index{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));border-block:1px solid var(--line);margin-bottom:16px}.workflow-index a{padding:20px 16px 20px 0;font-size:13px}.workflow-index span{display:block;font:10px var(--mono);color:var(--phase-pos);margin-bottom:9px}.workflow-index a:hover{color:var(--phase-pos)}.workflow-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:50px 1.4fr 1fr;gap:38px;padding:58px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.workflow-row:last-of-type{border-bottom:0}.workflow-number{font:24px var(--mono);color:var(--phase-pos)}.workflow-row h2{font-size:32px;margin:14px 0}.workflow-row p{font-size:16px}.workflow-row aside{padding-left:30px;border-left:1px solid var(--line)}.workflow-row h3{font:11px var(--mono);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--phase-pos)}.workflow-row aside p{font-size:14px}.workflow-row aside p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}.document-section{padding-top:45px}.document-section .card p{margin-bottom:22px}@media(max-width:750px){.workflow-index{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.workflow-row{grid-template-columns:30px 1fr;gap:20px;padding-block:40px}.workflow-row aside{grid-column:2;padding:0;border:0}.workflow-row h2{font-size:28px}}
</style>
